  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of collections of Ukrainian women artists, including Maria Prymachenko, and the development of a museum dedicated to recognizing the historical role played by Ukrainian female artists</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The destruction of the museum and the artworks of Prymachenko and other artists have raised significant concerns about the protection of cultural heritage amid the ongoing war. There is an urgent need to protect and promote artistic works, especially those by Ukrainian female artists. To address this, the current project has been initiated to restore Prymachenko&apos;s rescued works, enhance the capacities of museum professionals in preservation and digitization, develop educational and awareness programs, and create a virtual museum. Future phases will focus on building a dedicated virtual museum, an immersive exhibition of female artists, and planning for a new museum dedicated to Ukrainian art and women&#x2019;s creativity.</narrative>
  </description>
